  "findings": [
    "Input DMA completion uses status bit 0x08000000 and terminal bit 0x10000000, advances a ring index. No capture timestamp in the audited completion/status path.",
    "A02941F4 returns success without copying when source IoNode+4 is not 1. InputDataProc counts a capacity-qualified destination before calling this writer, then can advance the DMA consume index even though the source gate is closed.",
    "InputDataProc MakeUp and overwrite-warning branches compare ring indices; no video DSP clock is referenced in those branches.",
    "The stop/rearm marker stores a control word into DMA descriptor+0x14, not a timestamp.",
    "Buffer-to-encoder payload descriptors have 12-byte entries with pointer/size/terminal flag; no timestamp field was found in this bounded path."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Closed source plus available capacity is sufficient for discard/progress; no assertion that every closed or backpressured state discards.",
    "Input/encoder effect callbacks can be custom and are not fully analyzed here.",
    "MMIO startup, DMA scheduling and hardware clock correlation are not executed.",
    "A bounded absence of timestamps does not prove all firmware synchronization paths absent.",
    "No shared capture epoch, lip sync, one-minute prerecord or device behavior verified."
  ]
}
